# SE-PROJECT

Hospital appointment management system with:
- Django REST backend
- React + Vite frontend
- JWT-based authentication with role-based access

## Tech Stack

- Backend: Django, Django REST Framework, SimpleJWT
- Frontend: React, Vite, Axios, React Router
- Database: SQLite (default)

## Project Structure

- backend/backend: Django project root (manage.py location)
- backend/backend/api: API app (models, serializers, views)
- frontend: React app

## Prerequisites

- Python 3.10+
- Node.js 18+
- npm

## Backend Setup

1. Open terminal in backend project root:

	cd backend/backend

2. Create and activate virtual environment (if needed):

	python -m venv .venv
	.venv\Scripts\activate

3. Install dependencies:

	pip install -r ../requirements.txt

4. Run migrations:

	python manage.py migrate

5. Start backend server:

	python manage.py runserver

Backend default URL:
- http://127.0.0.1:8000

## Frontend Setup

1. Open terminal in frontend root:

	cd frontend

2. Install dependencies:

	npm install

3. Start frontend dev server:

	npm run dev

Frontend build:

	npm run build

## Environment Notes

Frontend API base URL can be set with:
- VITE_API_BASE

If not set, frontend uses:
- http://localhost:8000

## Authentication and Roles

Roles:
- patient
- doctor
- admin

Public self-registration allows:
- patient
- doctor

JWT endpoints:
- POST /api/auth/register/
- POST /api/auth/login/
- POST /api/auth/refresh/

## Core Features

- Role-based protected routes and APIs
- Doctor weekly availability and generated slots
- Appointment booking, cancellation, rescheduling
- Admin dashboard and user management
- Consultation reports by doctors

## Slot Capacity Rule

Each doctor slot now supports up to 15 appointments.

Details:
- Slots are considered available only while active appointments in that slot are less than 15.
- Active statuses for capacity are: pending, confirmed, completed.
- Cancelled appointments do not consume capacity.

## Important API Areas

- Doctors and slots:
  - GET /api/doctors/
  - GET /api/doctors/<doctor_id>/slots/
  - GET /api/slots/?doctor_id=<id>

- Appointments:
  - GET /api/appointments/
  - POST /api/appointments/book/
  - PATCH /api/appointments/<appointment_id>/cancel/
  - PATCH /api/appointments/<appointment_id>/reschedule/
  - PATCH /api/appointments/<appointment_id>/hide/
  - GET /api/appointments/today/

- Admin:
  - GET /api/admin/dashboard-summary/
  - GET /api/admin/users/
  - PATCH /api/admin/users/<user_id>/status/
  - POST /api/admin/doctors/<doctor_id>/remove/

## Common Commands

Backend checks:

	python manage.py check
	python manage.py showmigrations api

Frontend:

	npm run dev
	npm run build

## Troubleshooting

- If frontend shows auth or API errors:
  - Confirm backend is running on port 8000.
  - Confirm VITE_API_BASE matches backend URL.

- If Django reports model changes:
  - Run python manage.py makemigrations
  - Run python manage.py migrate

- If npm run dev fails:
  - Delete node_modules and package-lock.json
  - Run npm install again

